From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:54:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sessions): watch a session's pull requests until they're
 green

After an agent opens a PR, someone still has to babysit it: notice a red
check, a review or a merge conflict, and nudge the session to deal with it.
This adds an opt-in watch that does that for any harness, behind the
default-off `pr_watch` feature.

- A "Watch PRs" chip in the composer bar, next to the PR link, opens a
  popover with "All PRs in this session" (every PR it tracks now and any it
  opens later) and one box per open PR with its title, CI state and
  wake-ups used. Unchecking one PR while "All" is on keeps the rest. The
  chip reads "Watching N PRs" while active, so it replaces a header pill;
  the PR panel keeps a "Watch until green" switch bound to the same state.
- A per-server poller (`omnigent/server/pr_watch.py`) reads each watched
  PR through the same path as the Pull Requests panel (runner, else host,
  running the provider CLI with the host's account), so it adds no
  credentials; the server vouches for the PR and stores what the read
  reports, as it does for the panel. It reports failed checks on the head
  commit, comments and reviews from other accounts, and merge conflicts once
  each, coalesced
  across PRs into one `[System: PR watch ...]` message sent through the
  normal message path only while the session is idle. Only comments and
  reviews from the repository's owners, members and collaborators count;
  anyone else's text never reaches the agent. In "all" mode it enrols PRs
  as the session's linked list grows, skipping merged and closed ones. The
  list is the server's stored one, which the Pull Requests tab shows, so an
  unlink there ends the watch and a PR stored as merged or closed is skipped
  without asking the host. Until the server has imported the session's PRs
  from the host (the stored list may be partial then), the host's own list
  decides.
- Each PR's watch ends with a transcript note that starts no turn when its
  checks pass with no changes requested, it is merged or closed, its
  wake-up budget (default 10) is spent, checks cannot be read, or five
  wake-ups in a row could not be delivered. The ended state is kept so
  "all" mode does not pick the PR up again.
- State lives in server-reserved session labels, so it survives a restart
  without a migration: `omnigent.pr_watch.mode` for "all", and a URL and a
  state label per PR keyed by a hash of its URL (values are capped at 256
  characters). Forks drop the whole family, and clients cannot write it
  except through GET/PUT/PATCH/DELETE /v1/sessions/{id}/pr-watch, which
  needs edit access to change.
- The GitHub payload gains `mergeable`, each reviewer's `submitted_at`,
  and comment and review `author_association`, so conflicts, repeat
  reviews and trusted authors are detectable.

Interval and budget: OMNIGENT_PR_WATCH_INTERVAL_S (90) and
OMNIGENT_PR_WATCH_MAX_WAKES (10).

Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
